# Writing on ashwinviswamithiran.com

This repo is public. Keep it to what is already public.

1. Never invent a fact, number, tool, title or date. If a claim can't be traced to the repo, a public source or Ashwin, ask him.
2. First person, plain, engineering framing. No hype words, no "passionate", no "excited to".
3. Never publish internal identifiers: hostnames, account or resource names, secret names, colleague or vendor-contact names, or contract values.
4. The employer is named only in the About section.
5. No novelty claims for promptlsh or adversarial-ai-cti. Related prior work is complementary and credited.
6. Don't describe the mechanism of any technique that isn't already published here. Ask first.
7. Titles exactly as on the resume. Don't claim to lead a team.
8. Upstream contributions are "filed" until they are merged.
9. Never commit private career notes, job-search material or internal documents to this repo.
10. If a claim is unsure, flag it to Ashwin rather than softening or inflating it.
